  "details": "Adding packages to a project can take a while (even worse on low-end pcs), and while this has of course improved a lot with updates, there is no visual indication that something is actually happening during the process. If a package takes a particularly long time to add to your project it can feel like VCC has just frozen. A progress bar would be a better indicator than the current design (grayed out buttons and a throbber- both of which can remind the user of the dreaded \"not responding\")",
